#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&koshell; is a framework in which you can work with several &koffice; "
"applications in the same window. Being based on a true component framework "
"&koshell; provides exactly the same functionality as the stand-alone "
"applications, and adds more features, by making available all components in "
"the same window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&koshell; is part of the &koffice; productivity suite for the K Desktop "
"Environment. Other applications in &koffice; include:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; (A full featured <acronym>WYSIWYG</acronym> (What You See Is What "
"You Get) Word-processor/Desktop Publishing Program.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kspread; (A spreadsheet application.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpresenter; (A presentation creator.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kexi; (An integrated environment for databases.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kivio; (A flowchart creator.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "<application>&karbon14;</application> (A vector drawing program.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "&krita; (A pixel based drawing program.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kchart; (A chart and graph creator.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kformula; (A formula editor.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kugar; (A report generation tool.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"See the individual application manuals for details on how to use them. These "
"manuals apply to running the applications as components inside &koshell; "
"just as well as running them stand-alone."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &koshell; Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "General"
msgstr "General"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&koshell; consists in a friendly workspace to allow you to work on several "
"&koffice; applications at the same time. In the &koshell; main window you "
"can see a side pane on the left showing the icons of the available &koffice; "
"components and the main view on the right which contains the main window of "
"the active component and the usual menubar and toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &koshell; when you start it for the first time"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "&koshell; screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can see &koshell; as it is the first time you run it. &koshell; "
"always starts empty. You can then choose different actions. You can use the "
"side pane on the left to open the programs as if they are standalone "
"applications. You can also open any supported document via the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice> menu and the corresponding &koffice; application will open with "
"the document loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also import any supported document using the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Import</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice> menu and as with the Open action, the adequate &koffice; "
"application will be used to load your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "Side Pane"
msgstr "Panèl lateral"

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&koshell;'s Side Pane</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&koshell;'s Side Pane</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>&koshell;'s Side Pane</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The side pane allows you to open a new &koffice; component as if it was the "
"stand-alone application. In most components, you are asked what document you "
"want to open, a template, an empty document or an existing document. The "
"main window of the component is then shown and the menubar, toolbars and "
"status bar in &koshell; are adapted to reflect the functionality of the "
"active component."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change the size of the icons in the side pane. Right-clicking on the "
"side pane will give you the option to use Large, Normal, or Small icons, as "
"well as the option to use text only instead of icons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you dislike the sidebar, you can simply hide it by dragging the splitter "
"to the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The view on the right which takes up most of the area of the &koshell; main "
"window shows the active component. This exactly corresponds to the main "
"window the component uses when run as a stand-alone application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&koshell;'s Main View</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:176
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&koshell;'s Main View</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>&koshell;'s Main View</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a component is loaded, the component own menus are merged with the "
"&koshell; menus and the component toolbars are added on the workspace."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each new component is opened in a new tab. Using the &RMB; on each tab "
"title, you can save the document in that tab or close that tab. The small "
"button on the right bottom with a red cross also allows you to close the "
"current tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A special action common to all components is the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> action in &koshell; "
"menubar. It opens the <guilabel>Insert Object</guilabel> dialog which starts "
"the &koffice; component as if it was a stand-alone application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&koshell; Insert Object dialog</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

